{"raw": {"https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Minnesota_State_Careers/job/St-Cloud/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Counselor-Education--State-University-Faculty_JR0000005883": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Counselor Education -State University Faculty", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Assistant/Associate Professor of Counselor Education -State University Faculty Institution: St. Cloud State University Classification Title: State University Faculty Bargaining Unit / Union: 209: Inter Faculty Organization City: St. Cloud FLSA: Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Unclassified - Unlimited Academic Salary Range: $64,963.00 - $193,146.00 Job Description Minnesota needs clinical mental health counselors and school counselors, and this program prepares them.\u00a0 We are looking for a counselor educator who wants real influence over how that happens.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 The Clinical Mental Health Counseling and School Counseling programs at St. Cloud State University invite applications for a tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Counselor Education, beginning August 16th, 2027. \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 We are a small faculty running daytime cohort programs with our own on-campus training clinic, live supervision, and a set of community partnerships that are already operating and open to a new colleague\u2019s ideas.\u00a0 Because the faculty is small, your voice on curriculum, clinical training, and program direction will matter from your first semester \u2013 not your seventh year.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 We are open on specialty. We are seeking an excellent counselor who can contribute broadly across the CACREP core curriculum, not a candidate in any single subfield. Your particular clinical and scholarly expertise \u2013 whatever it is \u2013 will help determine what we build next.\u00a0 \u00a0 How teaching works here. \u00a0 \u00a0 A 3/3 graduate load . Graduate courses are weighted at 4 credits in the 24-credit IFO academic year-some clinical courses at five -, so a full graduate load is 6 courses per year rather than 8.\u00a0 \u00a0 Daytime only. Our programs run on a cohort model with daytime classes.\u00a0 Students know their full schedule from admission to graduation, and so do you. In counselor education, where evening teaching is the norm, this is unusual.\u00a0 \u00a0 No faculty member owns a course. Faculty submit teaching preferences annually. If you want to teach a course several years running to develop it, you can.\u00a0 If you want to move into something new, you can. We deliberately distribute the first-year content sequence \u2013 the heaviest teaching in the program, with intensive skills feedback and the beginning of gatekeeping \u2013 across the whole faculty rather than concentrating it on newer colleagues.\u00a0 \u00a0 You follow a cohort through its full three-year life cycle. \u00a0 You teach students in their first year, again in practicum, and through internship to graduation.\u00a0 Most programs don\u2019t work this way, and it takes some getting\u00a0 used to. We do it because when you make a gatekeeping decision or write a recommendation, you\u2019re drawing on three years of watching someone develop rather than one semester\u2019s impression.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 A cohort\u2019s first year typically includes Introduction to the profession, Ethics, Assessment in Counseling, Multicultural Counseling, and Counseling Procedures/Skills and either diagnosis and treatment planning or child/adolescent counseling.\u00a0 \u00a0 Summer is optional, and it\u2019s yours. \u00a0 We poll students at orientation about which electives they want, and together with our advisory board build a 3-year summer rotation from that data.\u00a0 Faculty teach in their own areas of interest, so this is where specialization lives \u2013 the core curriculum is taught by everyone, and the summer sequence is where your expertise becomes curriculum. Because the rotation is built from student demand and planned three years out, you\u2019ll know your summer teaching well in advance.\u00a0 Additional summer sections are also regularly available in our undergraduate program.\u00a0 Summer teaching is compensated separately from the academic year contract under Article 13 of the IFO agreement.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Clinical training \u00a0 Students complete practicum on campus in the College of Education, Health & Human Sciences training clinic, with live bug-in-the-ear supervision.\u00a0 You\u2019ll supervise in real time rather than from recordings \u2013 and you\u2019ll have a clinical setting available for your own scholarship.\u00a0 \u00a0 Students who want to specialize working with children and adolescents also have the opportunity for a community- partner practicum placement.\u00a0 \u00a0 Faculty and students work across a set of interdisciplinary collaborations that are already running, including integrated behavioral health initiatives, support for first-year nursing students, programming for students' parents, support for international students, support for the campus counseling center, support for campus/community serving autism clinic and for campus/clinic communication/sciences disorder clinic, and youth programming in partnership with the YMCA.\u00a0 You would join active partnerships rather than build from zero.\u00a0 \u00a0 Scholarship \u00a0 \u00a0 Our tenure process is outlined in the IFO contract.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Our training clinic, our community partnerships, and our three-year cohort structure are all available as research settings.\u00a0 We support applied and community-engaged scholarship alongside traditional peer-reviewed work, and we treat dissertation-derived publication as legitimate early scholarship.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Faculty receive professional development funding under the IFO contract, are eligible for sabbatical, and have access to a range of internal grant programs.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Why this position is different. \u00a0 \u00a0 Your workload has been thought about. \u00a0 A 3/3 load.\u00a0 Daytime teaching only.\u00a0 Course assignment by annual preference, with no one owning a course.\u00a0 An optional summer sequence in your own area of interest.\u00a0 \u00a0 Your influence is proportional to our size. \u00a0 On a faculty of 6, a new colleague\u2019s ideas about curriculum and clinical training get implemented rather than queued.\u00a0 You will shape this program from your first year, not your seventh year.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Your specialty gets six credits of its own. \u00a0 Whatever you bring \u2013 trauma, addictions, couples and family work, career, group work, integrated behavioral health, counseling children and adolescents, or something we don\u2019t currently offer \u2013 there\u2019s a place to build it into curriculum.\u00a0 \u00a0 Our graduates fill a real regional need. \u00a0 Central Minnesota\u2019s behavioral health workforce depends on programs like ours.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Our program at a glance \u00a0 Accreditation: CACREP-accredited on 2024 standards.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Model: Cohort-based, daytime, on-campus master\u2019s programs in CMHC and School Counseling\u00a0 Cohort size: \u00a0 [#] has grown equal with growth in faculty hire.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Faculty: [6] Counselor faculty, with expertise in [Social Justice and Cultural fluency, addictions, group work, complex trauma]\u00a0 Student outcomes: Link to our last CAPER\u00a0 Home: Department of Behavioral Health and Counseling, School of Education, Health and Human Sciences.\u00a0 Degrees: \u00a0 Master\u2019s-level CMHC, School Counseling, Graduate Certificate in Addictions (non CACREP) and upcoming 3+3.\u00a0 We do not offer a doctorate in counselor education at this time; our faculty teach and advise at the master\u2019s level.\u00a0 Our program's trajectory We turn away qualified applicants every year. \u00a0 Our graduate program receives more applications than we have seats and has for 10 years running.\u00a0\u00a0 We sit in a college built around exactly this kind of work. \u00a0 The College of Education, Health & Human Sciences brings education, health, and human sciences together under one roof with an emphasis on field-based learning and alignment with regional workforce needs.\u00a0\u00a0 The infrastructure is built. Our on-campus training clinic with live supervision, our community partnerships, and our clinical placement network are established and operating. Living here St. Cloud is a city of about 70,000 on the Mississippi River, roughly 60 miles northwest of Minneapolis-St. Paul.\u00a0 Housing costs are a fraction of metro rates and commutes are measured in minutes, so a faculty salary goes considerably further here than in the Twin Cities or on either coast.\u00a0 The region has a substantial healthcare and behavioral health sector, which matters if you are relocating with a partner in the field.\u00a0 SCSU also operates a campus in the Twin Cities metro, if a metro-area residence suits you better. \u00a0 *Employment for this position is covered by the collective bargaining agreement for the Inter Faculty Organization (IFO), which can be found at:\u00a0 https://www.ifo.org/contract \u00a0 Salary: *The salary range is the contractual range; however, salary upon hire is dependent upon qualifications and experience. Minimum Qualifications Earned doctorate in Counselor Education from a CACREP-accredited program.\u00a0 ABD candidates will be considered if the degree will be conferred by August 1st, 2027.\u00a0 Licensed as an LPC/LPCC/LMHC or license-eligible in the State of Minnesota. If not licensed, able to submit application for licensure upon the semester of hire. https://mn.gov/boards/behavioral-health/ or a licensed school counselor or license-eligible for a tier 3 or 4 license in MN upon the semester of hire. Counseling experience sufficient to teach and supervise master\u2019s level counseling students. Evidence of professional identity as a counselor educator \u2013 for example, membership and service in ACA, ACES, or a division; supervision credentialing; or scholarship in counselor preparation. Demonstrated effectiveness in teaching, supervising, or mentoring students from a range of backgrounds and life experiences. Preferred Qualification\u00a0 Clinical or scholarly expertise in any area that would extend our current faculty strengths \u2013 including, but not limited to, trauma and crisis response, addictions and co-occurring disorders, couples and family counseling, career development, group work, assessment, integrated behavioral health, rural mental health, school counseling, or counseling children and adolescents. Approved Clinical Supervisor (ACS) credential and/or equivalent supervision training and experience and/or board-approved supervisor status. Experience with CACREP self-study process, either in a self-study or as a site team reviewer. Certification or advanced training in a clinical/counseling modality (for example, Play Therapy, DBT, EMDR, TF-CBT, MI). An active scholarly agenda with evidence of, or clear potential for, peer-reviewed publication and presentation schedule. We do not expect any candidate to meet every preferred qualification.\u00a0 If you meet the required qualifications and the position interests you, we want to hear from you.\u00a0 \u00a0 Other Requirements We ask for three items now.\u00a0 To reduce the burden of applying, an initial application consists of three items: 1. Curriculum Vitae: If ABD, including your scheduled defense date and\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 anticipated degree conferral date. 2. Cover Letter: describe your teaching, scholarship, counseling background, \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 and what draws you to this position. 3. Contact information for two (3) current, professional references.\u00a0 Note: We\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 will not contact references without your permission. Candidates invited to a first-round interview will be asked for a teaching philosophy statement, a sample of scholarship or creative work, and unofficial graduate transcripts.\u00a0 Official transcripts are required of finalists.\u00a0 Please note that successful applicants must be eligible to work in the United States on or before the effective date of appointment. Eligibility includes being a U.S. citizen or national, a lawful permanent resident, or a foreign national authorized to work in the U.S. without the need for employer sponsorship. Employees must maintain work authorization without sponsorship for the duration of their appointment. Work Shift (Hours / Days of work) Please note that successful applicants must be eligible to work in the United States on or before the effective date of appointment. Eligibility includes being a U.S. citizen or national, a lawful permanent resident, or a foreign national authorized to work in the U.S. without the need for employer sponsorship. Employees must maintain work authorization without sponsorship for the duration of their appointment. Telework (Yes/No) Varies About St. Cloud State University serves close to 10,000 students and is committed to providing accessible, high-quality education that prepares graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Located along the Mississippi River in St. Cloud, Minnesota, SCSU combines personalized support, applied learning, research, and community engagement to create opportunities for students, employees, and the region. With more than 133,000 alumni worldwide, SCSU continues to make a lasting impact through education, innovation, and service. \u00a0 St. Cloud State University is committed to creating an inclusive and welcoming environment that values the unique contributions of all students, faculty, staff, and community members. We recognize that welcoming a variety of perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds strengthens our teaching, learning, research, and service mission. We encourage applications from individuals who share our commitment to student success, belonging, and excellence. \u00a0 Employment for this position is covered by the collective bargaining agreement for the IFO which can be found at: https://www.ifo.org/ St. Cloud State University is committed to excellence and actively supports cultural diversity. To promote this endeavor, we invite individuals who contribute to such diversity to apply, including minorities, women, LGBTQIA+, persons with disabilities and veterans. St. Cloud State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, creed, religion, age, national origin, disability, marital status, status with regards to public assistance, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or status as a U.S. veteran. The Interim Title IX coordinator at St. Cloud State University is Andrea Rooney. For additional information, contact the Office of Institutional Equity & Access, (320) 308-5123, Admin. Services Bldg. Rm 121\u00a0 Salary is commensurate with experience and qualifications and is subject to the terms and conditions of the applicable bargaining unit agreement or personnel plan. Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website. \u00a0 To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 08-16-2027 Position End Date: Open Date: 10-12-2026 Close Date: 11-30-2026 Posting Contact Name: Courtney Marie Graber Posting Contact Email: courtney.graber@stcloudstate.edu"}, "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Minnesota_State_Careers/job/St-Cloud/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Nursing--Full-Time-Probationary--Tenure-Track----Maternal-and-Child-Health-Focus-State-University-Faculty_JR0000005794": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing, Full-Time Probationary (Tenure Track) - Maternal and Child Health Focus-State University Faculty", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing, Full-Time Probationary (Tenure Track) - Maternal and Child Health Focus-State University Faculty Institution: St. Cloud State University Classification Title: State University Faculty Bargaining Unit / Union: 209: Inter Faculty Organization City: St. Cloud FLSA: Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Unclassified - Unlimited Academic Salary Range: $64,963.00 - $193,146.00 Job Description Join the Department of Nursing Science at St. Cloud State University \u00a0 The Department of Nursing Science invites applications for a full-time, probationary (tenure-track) Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing beginning January 2027. We seek a collaborative nurse educator committed to preparing practice-ready baccalaureate nurses and contributing to a student-centered academic community. The primary teaching need for this search is maternal and child health nursing; opportunities may also exist to teach across the undergraduate curriculum based on candidate expertise and departmental needs.\u00a0 \u00a0 Candidates with a completed doctorate, those currently pursuing a doctorate, and master\u2019s-prepared nurses interested in continued academic and professional development are encouraged to apply.\u00a0 \u00a0 This is an in-person faculty position based on the St. Cloud State University campus in St. Cloud, Minnesota. Regular on-campus presence is required. The successful candidate will join faculty who value strong clinical partnerships, applied learning, clinical judgment, simulation, evidence-based practice, and preparation for contemporary nursing practice. Teaching assignments may include classroom, laboratory, simulation, clinical, hybrid, and online learning environments based on departmental and program needs.\u00a0 \u00a0 St. Cloud State University is committed to effective teaching and student success. Faculty are expected to engage in ongoing professional development and, as appropriate to the appointment, scholarly achievement, continued preparation and study, student growth and development, and service to the university and community.\u00a0 Department of Nursing Science: https://www.stcloudstate.edu/nursing/ Inter Faculty Organization collective bargaining agreement: https://www.ifo.org/ \u00a0*The salary range is the contractual range; however, salary upon hire is dependent upon qualifications and experience. Position Overview \u00a0 The Department of Nursing Science offers a pre-licensure Bachelor of Science in Nursing program and a fully online RN-BS Completion Program. The pre-licensure program is accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE) and approved by the Minnesota Board of Nursing. Educational and clinical experiences prepare graduates to provide person-centered nursing care in diverse and rapidly changing health care environments.\u00a0 The department emphasizes clinical judgment, evidence-based practice, quality and safety, interprofessional collaboration, population health, professional identity, and preparation for the NCLEX-RN. Students learn through classroom, clinical, simulation, laboratory, and technology-enhanced experiences, supported by the Jim and Ann Marie Maciej Nursing Education Suite and strong regional clinical partnerships.\u00a0 Primary Responsibilities \u00a0 \u2022 Teach undergraduate nursing courses in classroom, clinical, simulation, and/or online environments, with a primary anticipated focus in general acute care nursing.\u00a0 \u2022 Support student learning, clinical judgment development, professional formation, and progression toward entry-level nursing practice.\u00a0 \u2022 Provide academic advising, mentoring, and guidance to undergraduate nursing students.\u00a0 \u2022 Collaborate with nursing faculty, staff, adjunct clinical faculty, preceptors, and community/clinical partners.\u00a0 \u2022 Participate in curriculum development, program evaluation, assessment of student learning, and continuous quality improvement.\u00a0 \u2022 Contribute to accreditation, regulatory, governance, and departmental service activities.\u00a0 \u2022 Engage in professional development, scholarly or creative activity, and service consistent with the expectations of a probationary faculty appointment and the IFO collective bargaining agreement.\u00a0 \u2022 Participate in departmental initiatives related to contemporary nursing education, including simulation, clinical judgment, the AACN Essentials, NCLEX-RN, and Next Generation NCLEX (NGN), as appropriate.\u00a0 \u00a0 Appointment at the Assistant or Associate Professor rank will be determined based on the successful candidate\u2019s education, academic and professional experience, scholarly accomplishments, and qualifications consistent with St. Cloud State University and Minnesota State policies and the applicable collective bargaining agreement\u00a0 \u00a0 Why Join SCSU Nursing? \u00a0 This position offers an opportunity to help educate the next generation of nurses while building an academic career within a collaborative department. Faculty benefit from strong relationships with regional health care and community partners, opportunities to teach across multiple learning environments, and meaningful engagement in curriculum innovation, simulation, clinical judgment, student mentoring, and professional service. The department especially welcomes experienced clinicians who are interested in bringing their practice expertise into nursing education.\u00a0 Minimum Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in nursing (MSN) from an accredited institution completed by the date of appointment.\u00a0 Current, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license in the United States and eligibility for Minnesota RN licensure by the date of appointment.\u00a0 Minimum of two years of professional nursing practice experience.\u00a0 Clinical knowledge or professional experience relevant to maternal and child health nursing and/or a related area of nursing practice.\u00a0 Demonstrated potential for effective teaching, clinical instruction, precepting, mentoring, staff development, or professional nursing education.\u00a0 Effective oral, written, interpersonal, and collaborative communication skills.\u00a0 Demonstrated ability to work effectively with students, colleagues, clinical partners, and individuals from diverse backgrounds.\u00a0 Commitment to student success and preparation of nurses for contemporary professional practice.\u00a0 Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in nursing or a related field (PhD, DNP, EdD), completed or in progress.\u00a0 Graduate preparation, certification, or substantial clinical expertise in maternal-newborn, women\u2019s health, pediatric, family, or related nursing practice.\u00a0 Teaching experience in a baccalaureate nursing program or other higher-education setting.\u00a0 Experience teaching in clinical, simulation, skills laboratory, online, hybrid, or technology-enhanced learning environments.\u00a0 Experience mentoring or precepting nursing students, new graduate nurses, or practicing nurses.\u00a0 Familiarity with contemporary nursing education frameworks and standards, including the AACN Essentials, clinical judgment, NCLEX-RN, and Next Generation NCLEX (NGN).\u00a0 Evidence of scholarly activity or demonstrated potential for scholarship appropriate to the faculty role.\u00a0 Experience with curriculum development, program assessment, accreditation, regulatory review, or academic service.\u00a0 Demonstrated interest in continued professional development and advancement as a nurse educator. Documents Needed to Apply Current curriculum vitae or resume.\u00a0 Cover letter addressing the minimum qualifications and describing the applicant\u2019s interest in the position, relevant nursing practice experience, teaching/mentoring experience or potential, and general acute care or related specialty expertise.\u00a0 Contact information for three professional references who can address the applicant\u2019s clinical expertise, teaching/mentoring effectiveness or potential, collaboration, and professional qualifications.\u00a0 Unofficial graduate transcripts. Official transcripts will be required if the candidate advances in the hiring process Other Requirements Please note that successful applicants must be eligible to work in the United States on or before the effective date of appointment. Eligibility includes being a U.S. citizen or national, a lawful permanent resident, or a foreign national authorized to work in the U.S. without the need for employer sponsorship. Employees must maintain work authorization without sponsorship for the duration of their appointment. Work Shift (Hours / Days of work) Varies About St. Cloud State University serves close to 10,000 students and is committed to providing accessible, high-quality education that prepares graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Located along the Mississippi River in St. Cloud, Minnesota, SCSU combines personalized support, applied learning, research, and community engagement to create opportunities for students, employees, and the region. With more than 133,000 alumni worldwide, SCSU continues to make a lasting impact through education, innovation, and service. St. Cloud State University is committed to creating an inclusive and welcoming environment that values the unique contributions of all students, faculty, staff, and community members. We recognize that welcoming a variety of perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds strengthens our teaching, learning, research, and service mission. We encourage applications from individuals who share our commitment to student success, belonging, and excellence. Employment for this position is covered by the collective bargaining agreement for IFO which can be found at: https://www.ifo.org/ St. Cloud State University is committed to excellence and actively supports cultural diversity. To promote this endeavor, we invite individuals who contribute to such diversity to apply, including minorities, women, LGBTQIA+, persons with disabilities and veterans. St. Cloud State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, creed, religion, age, national origin, disability, marital status, status with regards to public assistance, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or status as a U.S. veteran. The Interim Title IX coordinator at St. Cloud State University is Andrea Rooney. For additional information, contact the Office of Institutional Equity & Access, (320) 308-5123, Admin. Services Bldg. Rm 121\u00a0 Salary is commensurate with experience and qualifications and is subject to the terms and conditions of the applicable bargaining unit agreement or personnel plan. Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website. \u00a0 To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 01-05-2027 Position End Date: Open Date: 09-21-2026 Close Date: 10-21-2026 Posting Contact Name: Courtney Marie Graber Posting Contact Email: courtney.graber@stcloudstate.edu"}, "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Minnesota_State_Careers/job/St-Cloud/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Nursing--Full-Time-Probationary--Tenure-Track----General-Acute-Care-Nursing-Focus--State-University-Faculty_JR0000005797": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing, Full-Time Probationary (Tenure Track) - General Acute Care Nursing Focus -State University Faculty", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing, Full-Time Probationary (Tenure Track) - General Acute Care Nursing Focus -State University Faculty Institution: St. Cloud State University Classification Title: State University Faculty Bargaining Unit / Union: 209: Inter Faculty Organization City: St. Cloud FLSA: Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Unclassified - Unlimited Academic Salary Range: $64,963.00 - $193,146.00 Job Description There are 3 vacancies for this posting. The Department of Nursing Science invites applications for a full-time, probationary (tenure-track) Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing beginning January 2027. We seek a collaborative nurse educator committed to preparing practice-ready baccalaureate nurses and contributing to a student-centered academic community. The primary teaching need for this search is general acute care nursing; opportunities may also exist to teach across the undergraduate curriculum based on candidate expertise and departmental needs. \u00a0 \u00a0 Candidates with a completed doctorate, those currently pursuing a doctorate, and master\u2019s -prepared nurses interested in continued academic and professional development are encouraged to apply. \u00a0 \u00a0 This is an in-person faculty position based on the St. Cloud State University campus in St. Cloud, Minnesota. Regular on-campus presence is required . The successful candidate will join faculty who value strong clinical partnerships, applied learning, clinical judgment, simulation, evidence-based practice, and preparation for contemporary nursing practice. Teaching assignments may include classroom, laboratory, simulation, clinical, hybrid, and online learning environments based on departmental and program needs. \u00a0 \u00a0 St. Cloud State University is committed to effective teaching and student success. Faculty are expected to engage in ongoing professional development and, as appropriate to the appointment, scholarly achievement, continued preparation and study, student growth and development, and service to the university and community. \u00a0 Department of Nursing Science: https://www.stcloudstate.edu/nursing/ Inter Faculty Organization collective bargaining agreement: https://www.ifo.org/ Position Overview \u00a0 The Department of Nursing Science offers a pre-licensure Bachelor of Science in Nursing program and a fully online RN-BS Completion Program. The pre-licensure program is accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE) and approved by the Minnesota Board of Nursing. Educational and clinical experiences prepare graduates to provide person-centered nursing care in diverse and rapidly changing health care environments. \u00a0 The department emphasizes clinical judgment, evidence-based practice, quality and safety, interprofessional collaboration, population health, professional identity, and preparation for the NCLEX-RN. Students learn through classroom, clinical, simulation, laboratory, and technology-enhanced experiences, supported by the Jim and Ann Marie Maciej Nursing Education Suite and strong regional clinical partnerships. \u00a0 Primary Responsibilities \u00a0 \u2022 Teach undergraduate nursing courses in classroom, clinical, simulation, and/or online environments, with a primary anticipated focus in general acute care nursing. \u00a0 \u2022 Support student learning, clinical judgment development, professional formation, and progression toward entry-level nursing practice. \u00a0 \u2022 Provide academic advising, mentoring, and guidance to undergraduate nursing students. \u00a0 \u2022 Collaborate with nursing faculty, staff, adjunct clinical faculty, preceptors, and community/clinical partners. \u00a0 \u2022 Participate in curriculum development, program evaluation, assessment of student learning, and continuous quality improvement. \u00a0 \u2022 Contribute to accreditation, regulatory, governance, and departmental service activities. \u00a0 \u2022 Engage in professional development, scholarly or creative activity, and service consistent with the expectations of a probationary faculty appointment and the IFO collective bargaining agreement. \u00a0 \u2022 Participate in departmental initiatives related to contemporary nursing education, including simulation, clinical judgment, the AACN Essentials, NCLEX-RN, and Next Generation NCLEX (NGN), as appropriate . \u00a0 \u00a0 Appointment at the Assistant or Associate Professor rank will be determined based on the successful candidate\u2019s education, academic and professional experience, scholarly accomplishments, and qualifications consistent with St. Cloud State University and Minnesota State policies and the applicable collective bargaining agreement \u00a0 \u00a0 Why Join SCSU Nursing? \u00a0 This position offers an opportunity to help educate the next generation of nurses while building an academic career within a collaborative department. Faculty benefit from strong relationships with regional health care and community partners, opportunities to teach across multiple learning environments, and meaningful engagement in curriculum innovation, simulation, clinical judgment, student mentoring, and professional service. The department especially welcomes experienced clinicians who are interested in bringing their practice expertise into nursing education. \u00a0 \u00a0 Salary Range: *The salary range denoted is the contractual range; however, salary upon hire is dependent upon qualifications and experience. Minimum Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in nursing (MSN) from an accredited institution completed by the date of appointment. \u00a0 Current, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license in the United States and eligibility for Minnesota RN licensure by the date of appointment. \u00a0 Minimum of two years of professional nursing practice experience. \u00a0 Clinical knowledge or professional experience relevant to general acute care nursing and/or a related area of nursing practice. \u00a0 Demonstrated potential for effective teaching, clinical instruction, precepting, mentoring, staff development, or professional nursing education. \u00a0 Effective oral, written, interpersonal, and collaborative communication skills. \u00a0 Demonstrated ability to work effectively with students, colleagues, clinical partners, and individuals from diverse backgrounds. \u00a0 Commitment to student success and preparation of nurses for contemporary professional practice. \u00a0 Preferred Qualification\u00a0 Doctoral degree in nursing or a related field (PhD, DNP, EdD), completed or in progress. \u00a0 Graduate preparation, certification, or substantial clinical expertise in adult acute care, medical-surgical, critical care, emergency, progressive care, perioperative, or other related acute care nursing practice. \u00a0 Teaching experience in a baccalaureate nursing program or other higher-education setting . \u00a0 Experience teaching in clinical, simulation, skills laboratory, online, hybrid, or technology-enhanced learning environments. \u00a0 Experience mentoring or precepting nursing students, new graduate nurses, or practicing nurses. \u00a0 Familiarity with contemporary nursing education frameworks and standards, including the AACN Essentials, clinical judgment, NCLEX-RN, and Next Generation NCLEX (NGN). \u00a0 Evidence of scholarly activity or demonstrated potential for scholarship appropriate to the faculty role. \u00a0 Experience with curriculum development, program assessment, accreditation, regulatory review, or academic service. \u00a0 Demonstrated interest in continued professional development and advancement as a nurse educator. \u00a0 Documents Needed to Apply Current curriculum vitae or resume. \u00a0 Cover letter addressing the minimum qualifications and describing the applicant\u2019s interest in the position, relevant nursing practice experience, teaching/mentoring experience or potential, and general acute care or related specialty expertise . \u00a0 Contact information for three professional references who can address the applicant\u2019s clinical expertise , teaching/mentoring effectiveness or potential, collaboration, and professional qualifications. \u00a0 Unofficial graduate transcripts. Official transcripts will be required if the candidate advances in the hiring process. \u00a0 Other Requirements Successful completion of employment requirements established by St. Cloud State University and Minnesota State. The successful candidate must maintain RN licensure appropriate to assigned teaching responsibilities. \u00a0 Please note that successful applicants must be eligible to work in the United States on or before the effective date of appointment. Eligibility includes being a U.S. citizen or national, a lawful permanent resident, or a foreign national authorized to work in the U.S. without the need for employer sponsorship. Employees must maintain work authorization without sponsorship for the duration of their appointment. Work Shift (Hours / Days of work) Varies About St. Cloud State University serves close to 10,000 students and is committed to providing accessible, high-quality education that prepares graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Located along the Mississippi River in St. Cloud, Minnesota, SCSU combines personalized support, applied learning, research, and community engagement to create opportunities for students, employees, and the region. With more than 133,000 alumni worldwide, SCSU continues to make a lasting impact through education, innovation, and service. St. Cloud State University is committed to creating an inclusive and welcoming environment that values the unique contributions of all students, faculty, staff, and community members. We recognize that welcoming a variety of perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds strengthens our teaching, learning, research, and service mission. We encourage applications from individuals who share our commitment to student success, belonging, and excellence. Employment for this position is covered by the collective bargaining agreement for the IFO which can be found at: https://www.ifo.org/ St. Cloud State University is committed to excellence and actively supports cultural diversity. To promote this endeavor, we invite individuals who contribute to such diversity to apply, including minorities, women, LGBTQIA+, persons with disabilities and veterans. St. Cloud State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, creed, religion, age, national origin, disability, marital status, status with regards to public assistance, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or status as a U.S. veteran. The Interim Title IX coordinator at St. Cloud State University is Andrea Rooney. For additional information, contact the Office of Institutional Equity & Access, (320) 308-5123, Admin. Services Bldg. Rm 121\u00a0 Salary is commensurate with experience and qualifications and is subject to the terms and conditions of the applicable bargaining unit agreement or personnel plan. Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website. \u00a0 To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 01-05-2027 Position End Date: Open Date: 09-21-2026 Close Date: 10-21-2026 Posting Contact Name: Courtney Marie Graber Posting Contact Email: courtney.graber@stcloudstate.edu"}, "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Minnesota_State_Careers/job/St-Cloud/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Teacher-Development--Elementary-Education---State-University-Faculty_JR0000005799": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Teacher Development- Elementary Education - State University Faculty", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Assistant or Associate Professor of Teacher Development- Elementary Education - State University Faculty Institution: St. Cloud State University Classification Title: State University Faculty Bargaining Unit / Union: 209: Inter Faculty Organization City: St. Cloud FLSA: Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Unclassified - Unlimited Academic Salary Range: $64,963.00 - $193,146.00 Job Description Through their research, teaching, and service, the ideal candidate will demonstrate St. Cloud State's commitment to our mission and values, especially our responsibility for the holistic education of our diverse student population. This includes our commitments to social justice, equity, access , inclusion, and attention to the various components of student belonging. Applicants will be expected to establish and maintain \u00a0 professional goals to be outstanding teachers through the use of \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 research-based, best- practices, and innovative pedagogy. They \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 should be willing to participate in teaching using delivery methods such as in person, online and hybrid. They will regularly engage in ongoing professional development and innovation opportunities focused on pedagogica l and professional growth. \u00a0 \u00a0 Tenure track position in the Elementary Education program with \u00a0 expectations to: \u00a0 \u00a0 Provide university course instruction that models effective instruction in Elementary Education in the areas of curriculum and instruction, pedagogy, culturally and linguistically inclusive instruction, social studies methods, or literacy. \u00a0 Provide academic advising, student support , student advocacy , mentorship, and recruitment . \u00a0 Participate in departmental and program operation, addressing departmental and program enhancement, state and national accreditation and program assessment and review. \u00a0 Teach and work effectively with persons from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, including an asset approach to multilingualism. \u00a0 Engage in scholarly activity \u00a0 Salary Range: *The salary range denoted is the contractual range; however, salary upon hire is dependent upon qualifications and experience. Minimum Qualifications Doctorate in C & I, Elementary Education, or \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 related field. (ABD considered with degree to be completed before appointment date.) \u00a0 Holds or has recently held a K-6 elementary education license. \u00a0 Minimum of three years\u2019 experience as a licensed, full-time classroom teacher of record in a K-6, U.S. public, elementary school . \u00a0 Demonstrated ability to effectively utilize technology in instruction. \u00a0 Demonstrated ability to teach and work collaboratively and effectively with persons from culturally and/or linguistically diverse backgrounds. \u00a0 Preferred Qualification\u00a0 A record of teaching excellence at the university level with in the department of Elementary Education: c urriculum and in struction , p edagogy, cu lturally and l inguistically sustaining instruction, social studies methods or literacy . \u00a0 Minimum of five years\u2019 experience as a licensed, full-time classroom teacher of record in a K-6, U.S ., public, elementary school . \u00a0 Background or degree and successful experience in multi-lingual education. \u00a0 Demonstrated ability to effectively utilize technology in instruction for both university candidates and elementary classrooms including online or hyb rid teaching . \u00a0 Demonstrated scholarly activity, such as research studies, professional articles and/or professional presentations. \u00a0 Demonstrated effective experience with course design , instruction , and \u00a0 assessment aligned with Minnesota Standards of Effective Practice, and/or Minnesota Content Standards. \u00a0 Experience with academic advising, student support , mentorship, or recruitment . \u00a0 Required Documents to Apply Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Other Requirements Please note that successful applicants must be eligible to work in the United States on or before the effective date of appointment. Eligibility includes being a U.S. citizen or national, a lawful permanent resident, or a foreign national authorized to work in the U.S. without the need for employer sponsorship. Employees must maintain work authorization without sponsorship for the duration of their appointment. Work Shift (Hours / Days of work) Varies About St. Cloud State University serves close to 10,000 students and is committed to providing accessible, high-quality education that prepares graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Located along the Mississippi River in St. Cloud, Minnesota, SCSU combines personalized support, applied learning, research, and community engagement to create opportunities for students, employees, and the region. With more than 133,000 alumni worldwide, SCSU continues to make a lasting impact through education, innovation, and service. St. Cloud State University is committed to creating an inclusive and welcoming environment that values the unique contributions of all students, faculty, staff, and community members. We recognize that welcoming a variety of perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds strengthens our teaching, learning, research, and service mission. We encourage applications from individuals who share our commitment to student success, belonging, and excellence. Employment for this position is covered by the collective bargaining agreement for IFO which can be found at: https://www.ifo.org/ St. Cloud State University is committed to excellence and actively supports cultural diversity. To promote this endeavor, we invite individuals who contribute to such diversity to apply, including minorities, women, LGBTQIA+, persons with disabilities and veterans. St. Cloud State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, creed, religion, age, national origin, disability, marital status, status with regards to public assistance, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or status as a U.S. veteran. The Interim Title IX coordinator at St. Cloud State University is Andrea Rooney. For additional information, contact the Office of Institutional Equity & Access, (320) 308-5123, Admin. Services Bldg. Rm 121\u00a0 Salary is commensurate with experience and qualifications and is subject to the terms and conditions of the applicable bargaining unit agreement or personnel plan. Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website. \u00a0 To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 01-05-2027 Position End Date: Open Date: 09-21-2026 Close Date: 10-21-2026 Posting Contact Name: Courtney Marie Graber Posting Contact Email: courtney.graber@stcloudstate.edu"}, "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Minnesota_State_Careers/job/St-Cloud/Instructor-Assistant-Associate-Professor--Speech-Language--and-Hearing-Sciences--Fixed-Term---State-University-Faculty_JR0000005798": {"title": "Instructor/Assistant/Associate Professor, Speech Language, and Hearing Sciences, Fixed Term - State University Faculty", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Instructor/Assistant/Associate Professor, Speech Language, and Hearing Sciences, Fixed Term - State University Faculty Institution: St. Cloud State University Classification Title: State University Faculty Bargaining Unit / Union: 209: Inter Faculty Organization City: St. Cloud FLSA: Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Unclassified - Limited Academic (Fixed Term) Salary Range: $50,065.00 - $88,381.00 Job Description The Speech, Language, and Hearing Scienses (SLHS ) department is part of the College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at St. Cloud State University . The undergraduate bachelor\u2019s program is on-line asynchronous, which allows a diverse student demographic to be a part of our program. We train speech-language pathologists in our highly competitive, clinically focused CAA accredited master\u2019s program. We offer our students high-impact learning opportunities through our on-campus Speech-Language and Hearing Clinic, community partnerships, clinical research and much more. Our high quality, comprehensive clinical services in speech-language pathology and audiology have been a community asset for nearly seven decades. More Information about the department can be found at: http://www.stcloudstate.edu/csd \u00a0 \u00a0 Specific job duties include: Teaching graduates/undergraduate courses in Communication Sciences and Disorders, advising students, conducting research in area of expertise, participating in departmental and university committees and/or clinical supervision.\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Salary Range: *The salary range denoted is the contractual range; however, salary upon hire is dependent upon qualifications and experience. Minimum Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Speech-Language Pathology. \u00a0 Possesses CCC-SLP and eligible for the Minnesota licensure (MDH) . \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Worked a minimum of 9-months of full-time clinical experience after being awarded the CCC. \u00a0 Evidence of demonstrated ability to teach and work with persons from culturally diverse backgrounds.\u00a0 \u00a0 Preferred Qualification\u00a0 Experience across the life span and communication/feeding disorders.\u00a0 \u00a0 Bilingual proficiency . \u00a0 Experience in academic and clinical teaching (on-line, in-person) and/or practice with documented teaching effectiveness. \u00a0 Willing to work with highly motivated students in a CAA accredited speech language pathology department; good rapport with other professionals; experience and sensitivity in dealing effectively with students, clients, and their families. \u00a0 Familiar with the 2020 Standards and Implementation Procedures for the Certificate of Clinical Competence in Speech-Language Pathology. \u00a0 \u200b Documents Needed to Apply Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Other Requirements Please note that successful applicants must be eligible to work in the United States on or before the effective date of appointment. Eligibility includes being a U.S. citizen or national, a lawful permanent resident, or a foreign national authorized to work in the U.S. without the need for employer sponsorship. Employees must maintain work authorization without sponsorship for the duration of their appointment. Work Shift (Hours / Days of work) Varies About St. Cloud State University serves close to 10,000 students and is committed to providing accessible, high-quality education that prepares graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Located along the Mississippi River in St. Cloud, Minnesota, SCSU combines personalized support, applied learning, research, and community engagement to create opportunities for students, employees, and the region. With more than 133,000 alumni worldwide, SCSU continues to make a lasting impact through education, innovation, and service. St. Cloud State University is committed to creating an inclusive and welcoming environment that values the unique contributions of all students, faculty, staff, and community members. We recognize that welcoming a variety of perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds strengthens our teaching, learning, research, and service mission. We encourage applications from individuals who share our commitment to student success, belonging, and excellence. Employment for this position is covered by the collective bargaining agreement for IFO which can be found at: https://www.ifo.org/ St. Cloud State University is committed to excellence and actively supports cultural diversity. To promote this endeavor, we invite individuals who contribute to such diversity to apply, including minorities, women, LGBTQIA+, persons with disabilities and veterans. St. Cloud State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, creed, religion, age, national origin, disability, marital status, status with regards to public assistance, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or status as a U.S. veteran. The Interim Title IX coordinator at St. Cloud State University is Andrea Rooney. For additional information, contact the Office of Institutional Equity & Access, (320) 308-5123, Admin. Services Bldg. Rm 121\u00a0 Salary is commensurate with experience and qualifications and is subject to the terms and conditions of the applicable bargaining unit agreement or personnel plan. Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website. \u00a0 To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 01-05-2027 Position End Date: 05-11-2027 Open Date: 09-21-2026 Close Date: 10-21-2026 Posting Contact Name: Courtney Marie Graber Posting Contact Email: courtney.graber@stcloudstate.edu"}}, "rows": {"https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Minnesota_State_Careers/job/St-Cloud/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Counselor-Education--State-University-Faculty_JR0000005883": {"school_id": 688, "posting_url": "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Minnesota_State_Careers/job/St-Cloud/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Counselor-Education--State-University-Faculty_JR0000005883", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Counselor Education -State University Faculty", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Behavioral Health and Counseling, School of Education, Health and Human Sciences", "area_key_words": "Counselor Education; own areas of interest", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "2026-10-12"}, "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Minnesota_State_Careers/job/St-Cloud/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Nursing--Full-Time-Probationary--Tenure-Track----Maternal-and-Child-Health-Focus-State-University-Faculty_JR0000005794": {"school_id": 688, "posting_url": "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Minnesota_State_Careers/job/St-Cloud/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Nursing--Full-Time-Probationary--Tenure-Track----Maternal-and-Child-Health-Focus-State-University-Faculty_JR0000005794", "job_t